php5 (5.6.40+dfsg-0+deb8u23+local1) jessie-security; urgency=high

  * Unofficial rebuild of Freexian ELTS php5 5.6.40+dfsg-0+deb8u23.
  * Security fixes from the deb.sury.org php5.6 series (5.6.40-104),
    refreshed for jessie (NEWS hunks dropped):
    - CVE-2026-7261: use-after-free after header parsing failure with
      SOAP_PERSISTENCE_SESSION (GHSA-m33r-qmcv-p97q).
    - CVE-2026-7262: broken NULL check for Apache map values in SOAP
      (GHSA-hmxp-6pc4-f3vv).
    - CVE-2026-6735: XSS in the FPM status endpoint (GHSA-7qg2-v9fj-4mwv).
    - GH-22186: heap overflow in openssl_encrypt() with AES-WRAP-PAD
      (no effect against jessie's OpenSSL 1.0.1, which lacks
      EVP_CIPH_WRAP_MODE).
    - CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619: state corruption via bailout
      (GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w, GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp).

 -- Hüseyin Koyun <389171+hypertext@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200

